WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:05.420
From undersea battles to crime-solving Pokemon,
November was filled with exciting glimpses

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:06.560
of upcoming movies.

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:10.720
Here are all the November trailers that showcased
some of the best looking new films.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:15.900
Will the merc with a filthy mouth still bring
enough of his trademark charm in a PG-13 film?

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.199
That's the experiment 20th Century Fox is
running this December by releasing a cleaned

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.300
up version of Deadpool 2 for Christmas.

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:23.440
That should work.

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:26.740
"The first order of business is to get me
in front of Cable so I can pull all the f------

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:29.840
blood out of his body and fashion his bones
into holiday jewelry."

00:00:30.089 --> 00:00:33.960
Although to be honest, since you can't tell
what Ryan Reynolds' mouth is doing under that

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:37.340
mask, it can't be too hard to dub in some
more family-friendly jokes.

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:38.920
Just look at all the versions of this scene:

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:43.060
"ooh, yeah, your bullets.

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:44.960
They're really fast."

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:49.800
"Those bullets are like super fast."

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:54.360
“Ow.”

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:59.620
Once Upon a Deadpool will also apparently
feature some entirely new scenes featuring

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:03.860
Fred Savage back in his role as the little
kid in bed from The Princess Bride.

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:06.700
Check it out when Once Upon a Deadpool hits
theaters on December 12th.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:10.999
As the director of The Lord of the Rings,
Peter Jackson is a guy who knows a thing or

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:15.820
two about big, epic films, and few stories
fit that description better than Mortal Engines.

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:20.340
Although he won't be directing, Jackson is
producing and co-writing this dystopian story

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:23.660
about massive rolling cities that eat other
cities.

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:26.840
Because, really, what else would a giant city
eat?

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:28.540
Tuna fish sandwiches?

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:32.659
While we've had plenty of glimpses of Mortal
Engines in the past months, November saw an

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:36.249
extended trailer that focuses more on the
crazy world of the film.

00:01:36.249 --> 00:01:38.780
Take a look when Mortal Engines premieres
on December 14th.

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:44.300
After becoming the surprise star of Justice
League in 2017, Jason Momoa is back in the

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:48.850
role of Aquaman in a standalone movie that'll
see him fighting to save Atlantis from his

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:53.409
half-brother Orm and taking on a swarm of
deep-sea monsters called the Trench.

00:01:53.409 --> 00:01:55.340
Oh, and Black Manta is in there, too.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:59.479
It's clear that Warner Bros. has a lot of
faith in this movie, and all signs point to

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:02.980
an outrageously fun big-screen adventure for
DC fans.

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:05.320
After all the jokes at his expense

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:06.460
"Let’s go buddy!”

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:07.820
“I’m coming!”

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:09.040
“Hahaha”

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:11.400
“Last one to the party can't fly."

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.980
maybe Aquaman will finally get the last laugh.

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:17.080
You can take the dive when Aquaman arrives
on December 21st.

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:22.520
Keanu Reeves headlines this sci-fi thriller
as a scientist who finds himself in dire straits

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:24.620
after he clones his dead family.

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:26.240
"How could you do this?”

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:30.540
“… Because I love you."

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:35.830
Apparently, he broke some rules when he fired
up his big ol' clone oven, because now the

00:02:35.830 --> 00:02:37.580
government's gunning for him and his family.

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:39.580
What's a simple scientist to do?

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:42.780
Fight back to save his loved ones - again.

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:47.290
Replicas has been a long time coming - it
was announced in 2014 and began production

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:50.820
in 2016, marking a nearly five year journey
to the big screen.

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:52.440
Hopefully, it was worth the wait.

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:55.360
Replicas hits theaters on January 11th, 2019.

00:02:56.040 --> 00:03:00.660
M. Night Shyamalan's Glass is building a lot
of hype, and November's minute-long TV spot

00:03:00.670 --> 00:03:05.340
highlights Kevin Crumb's "Beast" persona and
more scenes from some kind of battle against

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:06.080
the police.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:09.620
Of course, being an M. Night Shyamalan film,
there's no doubt that Glass is going to feature

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:12.240
plenty of twists that aren't being touched
on in the trailers.

00:03:12.430 --> 00:03:16.820
Tellingly, none of the trailers show what
Mr. Glass is up to outside of that psychiatric

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:17.320
hospital.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:21.240
That's all the more reason to check it out
when Glass breaks into theaters on January

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:21.780
18th.

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:26.920
Serenity has equal potential to be either
a harrowing, mind-bending thriller or a whole

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:27.740
bunch of crap.

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:29.200
It's hard to tell at this point!

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:33.700
Matthew McConaughey stars as the captain of
a fishing boat enjoying the quiet island life

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:34.480
in the tropics.

00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:39.760
He's reunited with his Interstellar costar
Anne Hathaway, who asks him to kill her husband.

00:03:39.770 --> 00:03:44.200
From that launching point, the trailer dives
into a world of paranoia and backstabbing,

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:47.150
with hints that there's a bigger plotline
at work behind the scenes.

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:51.160
"This whole island's a part of it, but nobody
knows it."

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:57.040
Serenity was written and directed by Steven
Knight, who previously put out 2013's Locke,

00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:01.380
starring Tom Hardy, and wrote the screenplay
for David Cronenberg's Eastern Promises.

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:05.800
Look for Serenity to drop into theaters on
January 25th, 2019.

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:09.660
Right now, there are two camps when it comes
to Alita: Battle Angel.

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:13.040
On one side, people seem to be having a little
trouble dealing with the decision to make

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:15.020
Alita's eyes big and anime-like.

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:20.140
"So what do you say?

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:21.620
“I say no.

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:22.380
It's not art."

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:26.700
On the other side, you have people who are
genuinely excited to see the beloved manga

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:27.780
come to the big screen.

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:31.880
Ultimately, it'll come down to how well the
film handles the story.

00:04:31.889 --> 00:04:36.120
Sure, some of the CGI looks a little goofy,
and Alita's relationship with the boy in the

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:38.590
trailers smells a lot like high school melodrama.

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:43.140
"You are the most human person I have ever
met,"

00:04:44.980 --> 00:04:47.480
Fingers crossed that none of that will drag
the film down.

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:51.560
With both Robert Rodriguez and James Cameron
working behind the scenes to bring Alita to

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:55.480
life, there's still a chance this could be
one of the surprise hits of 2019.

00:04:55.720 --> 00:04:57.920
Find out when it lands on February 14th.

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:02.340
The future just got a whole lot more interesting
with the release of the second teaser for

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:03.260
Captive State.

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:07.920
Like the first teaser, this one showcases
a world in turmoil as humanity tries to win

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:10.820
back its freedom from a ruling class of extraterrestrials.

00:05:11.170 --> 00:05:15.300
Rise of the Planet of the Apes director Rupert
Wyatt is helming and co-writing the film,

00:05:15.310 --> 00:05:18.130
with Ashton Sanders and John Goodman starring.

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:19.640
Check it out in March 2019.

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:24.760
Ryan Reynolds is set to star in Detective
Pikachu, providing the weirdly deep voice

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:27.940
of Pokemon's iconic yellow electric mouse-thing.

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:32.960
"I know you can't understand me but put down the stapler or

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:36.840
I will electrocute you."

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:41.740
The story sees Pikachu teaming up with a young
man named Tim Goodman to find Goodman's father,

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:43.240
a detective who went missing.

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:47.340
Since Goodman is apparently the only human
who can understand what Pikachu is actually

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:51.680
saying, they have to work together to navigate
the magical world of adorable Pokemon critters

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:52.780
to solve the case.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:56.640
You gotta catch Detective Pikachu in theaters
on May 10th, 2019.

00:05:57.300 --> 00:06:01.960
It's been eight years since Toy Story 3 left
Buzz, Woody, and everyone else in the care

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:04.140
of little Bonnie while Andy left for college.

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:07.760
It was an ending that was both heartbreaking
and heartwarming, and it made the perfect

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:11.360
close to the relationship between Andy and
the lovable gang of toys.

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:12.720
Until now.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:18.160
Disney/Pixar is bringing them back into our
lives in 2019 with Toy Story 4, which will

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:22.330
follow the toys on a new adventure that hopefully
will be just as touching as the preceding

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:23.100
three films.

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:28.320
The main voice cast is returning, with Tom
Hanks and Tim Allen voicing Woody and Buzz,

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:28.820
respectively.

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:33.380
Hanks has remarked that the ending of Toy
Story 4 is particularly emotional.

00:06:33.380 --> 00:06:36.660
Get ready to weep openly in a movie theater
in June 2019.

00:06:37.240 --> 00:06:42.140
After months of anticipation, Disney finally
released the first trailer for their upcoming

00:06:42.140 --> 00:06:46.060
live-action remake of The Lion King - and
it kind of looks exactly like the original

00:06:46.060 --> 00:06:46.560
film.

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:51.940
The teaser mostly focuses on the opening scene
from the 1994 version, showing baby Simba

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:57.080
on Pride Rock as Rafiki anoints his head with
red baboon juice - or in this case, dust.

00:06:57.480 --> 00:07:02.040
Another shot the trailer shows is a sweeping
view of a herd of wildebeests stampeding into

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:06.040
a gorge while Mufasa's voice says, "The sun
will set on my time here."

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:10.729
That's clearly some not-so-subtle foreshadowing
that the 2019 movie will probably recreate

00:07:10.729 --> 00:07:14.980
the scene that made our six-year-old selves
realize that life was a meaningless void.

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:22.000
“ahh”

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:23.460
Anyway!

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:25.340
That new Simba sure does look cute!

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:29.840
We just can't wait for The Lion King to hit
theaters in July 2019.

